#: ../../../pro/reports/components_filters.md:5
msgid ""
"To write DataFrames in a consistent manner to Excel, xlwings Reports ignores "
"the DataFrame indices. If you need to pass the index over to Excel, reset "
"the index before passing in the DataFrame to `render_template`: `df."
"reset_index()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../pro/reports/components_filters.md:7
msgid ""
"When working with pandas DataFrames, the report designer often needs to "
"tweak the data. Thanks to filters, they can do the most common operations "
"directly in the template without the need to write Python code. A filter is "
"added to the placeholder in Excel by using the pipe character: "
"`{{ myplaceholder | myfilter }}`. You can combine multiple filters by using "
"multiple pipe characters: they are applied from left to right, i.e. the "
"result from the first filter will be the input for the next filter. Let's "
"start with an example before listing each filter with its details:"
msgstr ""

